80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (ACM-W is the Association for Computing Machinery committee on Women in Computing. It celebrates, informs and supports women in computing, and works with the ACM-W community of computer scientists, educators, employers and policymakers to improve working and learning environments for women.  )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
