82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (The RPI chapter of ACM-W strives to recruit, engage, and rejoice in the accomplishments of gender minority computer scientists within the institute. By providing a variety of workshops, networking events, and career advancement opportunities, the chapter strives to create equal opportunity and diversification in CS-related fields.  We welcome all women and gender minorities who are interested in computing and related fields to be a part of our chapter. We strive to be a safe space for people of all backgrounds, sexual orientations and gender identities.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
